  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster is primarily driven by mid-day consolidation traps (10:30\u201311:15 IST entries on NTPC, TATASTEEL, and AXISBANK) where 2.0x volume sweeps lacked institutional follow-through and reversed into tight 0.45%\u20130.65% stops. Furthermore, trades #3 (ICICIBANK) and #9 (AXISBANK) moved favorably to trigger the 1.0R breakeven stop (+0.12% gross gain), only to be whipsawed on minor pullbacks where statutory transaction fees turned positive gross P&L into net losses. Overall, the system is suffering from severe fee drag (\u20b950.94 in fees vs \u20b9-29.13 net P&L) due to premature breakeven stops and low-conviction mid-morning entries.",
    "learning": "In NSE cash equities, setting a breakeven trigger at 1.0R on tight stops (~0.45%\u20130.50%) invites mean-reversion noise to clip the position before trend expansion, turning winning setups into fee-induced net losses; higher volume conviction (2.4x+) and wider structural breathing room are required to survive mid-day liquidity regimes.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.35,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.4,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.25,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #87 Quantitative Review & Parameter Mutation\nForensic analysis of Cycle #87 revealed that strategy profitability is being eroded by transaction fee drag (`\u20b950.94` fees against `\u20b921.81` gross profit) and mid-morning (10:30\u201311:15 IST) false breakouts in heavyweights like `NTPC` and `TATASTEEL`. Specifically, the `1.0R` breakeven trigger prematurely choked winning trades (`ICICIBANK`, `AXISBANK`) during routine intraday pullbacks, converting gross gains into net fee losses. To mitigate noise whipsaws and filter out low-conviction mid-day liquidity sweeps, we are elevating `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` from `2.0x` to `2.4x` and widening `min_sl_pct` to `0.55%`. Concurrently, `breakeven_trigger_r` is pushed to `1.25R` alongside a `1.35%` `min_target_pct` to ensure winning trades expand sufficiently to comfortably absorb NSE statutory brokerage and STT charges."
  },
